  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "In some languages the choice between **come** and **go** depends only on movement toward the speaker. English usually also uses **come** for movement toward the listener, or to a place where the listener will be: *I'll come to your office at three.*",
    "grammar": "The past participle is the same as the base form: *she has come*, not *she has came*.",
